        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-024','title':'MISS applicability with no printed Intruder-type badges','decisionClass':'source-ambiguity-owner-decision-after-source-search','blocksRuleIds':ATTACK_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-024'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['docs/rules/semantics/attack-source-index.json','docs/rules/open-questions.md:SEM-Q-024'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-024-A','description':'A no-badge MISS panel applies universally to Adult, Drone, and Queen Attacks.','support':'licensed record explicitly lists all three types; scan layout likely uses omission as universal, but no checked official convention says so'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-024-B','description':'No matching badge means no associated effect; the scan card is discarded without reshuffling.','support':'official Standard Attacks instruct finding a matching type icon'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-024-C','description':'Another source-local universal-applicability convention applies.','support':'the face visibly has text but no printed badge or explanatory marker'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-025','title':'Queen Health trigger timing inside Shoot, Burst, and other Actions','decisionClass':'official-clarification-preferred','blocksRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-025'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['docs/rulebooks/rulebook_text.txt:lines 5514–5537, 5576–5605, 5747–5763','docs/rules/source-extraction/faq-v1.2-source-extraction.json:FQ-P02-U03','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-025-A','description':'Resolve the Queen Health card immediately when the marker reaches the final space or an applicable lethal Shoot result occurs, then continue only the still-legal non-Hit remainder of the Action while ignoring all later Hits.','support':'page 35 says “Whenever” the marker reaches the final space and explicitly ignores further Hits in that Action; exact continuation position is not stated'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-025-B','description':'Finish the enclosing Shoot/Burst die, Hit allocation, and printed Weapon/Action operations first, then resolve one Queen Health card for the trigger.','support':'Combat procedures present complete ordered Action steps, while page 35 does not explicitly interrupt those steps'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-025-C','description':'Use another source-defined interrupt window that distinguishes the initial Shoot Hit, lethal die result, Burst Hits, and additional-effect operations.','support':'FAQ confirms when a Shoot is lethal but does not define this nested timing window'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-026','title':'Attribution of “If the card was drawn by a Character” on Queen Health faces','decisionClass':'source-ambiguity-owner-decision-after-source-search','blocksRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-026'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['assets/tts-mod/extract/selected-card-text-evidence.json','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json','docs/rulebooks/rulebook_text.txt:lines 3095–3100, 5747–5763'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-026-A','description':'The Character whose Action/effect dealt the triggering Hit is the drawing Character and owns any Character-bound lower-panel context.','support':'the faces condition their effects on a Character draw and Command rules retain an effect owner, but the card does not define attribution'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-026-B','description':'Only a direct Character-controlled Combat Action counts; non-Action, commanded, Fire, Event, or other sources draw through the rules system and fail the condition.','support':'possible literal distinction between a Character draw and a non-player effect; no checked source enumerates qualifying sources'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-026-C','description':'The physical player who reveals/draws the top card counts regardless of which effect caused the Queen Health trigger.','support':'possible tabletop handling reading, but physical handling is not named as rules ownership'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-027','title':'Queen death timing when the final card is drawn versus discarded','decisionClass':'official-clarification-preferred','blocksRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-027'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['docs/rulebooks/rulebook_text.txt:lines 5754–5772','docs/rules/source-extraction/objective-help-sheet.json:P1-GT-06/P2-GT-06','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-027-A','description':'The Queen dies only when a Queen Health card enters the discard pile; merely drawing the last deck card does not trigger death before its bottom effect and final discard.','support':'page 35 repeatedly says the last card is discarded and explicitly sequences the drawn-card discard after its bottom effect'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-027-B','description':'The Queen dies as soon as drawing leaves the Queen Health deck empty, before additional discards or the bottom effect, while the bottom effect still resolves under the page-35 exception.','support':'both Objective Help occurrences define Queen death when the deck is empty'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-027-C','description':'Additional hidden discards can kill the Queen before the bottom effect, but drawing the final card uses a separate source-defined timing point later in the resolution.','support':'page 35 explicitly mentions death caused by additional discards but does not reconcile the drawn-final-card empty-deck case'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-028','title':'Malfunction-or-Unreinforce branch ownership and location handling','decisionClass':'source-ambiguity-owner-decision-after-source-search','blocksRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-028'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['assets/tts-mod/extract/v2-dl/tree/cards/game/queenHealthDeck-041.png','assets/tts-mod/extract/selected-card-text-evidence.json','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json','docs/rulebooks/rulebook_text.txt:lines 4150–4157, 4368–4375, 4414–4426'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-028-A','description':'The attributed drawing Character chooses one legal branch; Malfunction targets the Queen’s Room and Unreinforce targets her current reinforced Corridor.','support':'the face prints OR, but names no owner and does not state whether either branch may be chosen regardless of Queen location'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-028-B','description':'Queen location deterministically dispatches the effect: Malfunction if she is in a Room, Unreinforce if she is in a Corridor.','support':'each branch names one mutually exclusive Queen location, but the card does not state “if” or otherwise define this dispatch'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-028-C','description':'Apply another physical/source-defined branch rule, including what happens when the Room already has a Malfunction or the Corridor is not reinforced and which nonzero face appears after Unreinforce.','support':'generic Malfunction fallback is defined, but Unreinforce and whole-branch legality are not'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-029','title':'Queen Hits terminal and inline local-glyph identity/scope','decisionClass':'official-clarification-preferred','blocksRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-029'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['docs/rules/source-extraction/rulebook-visual-obligations.json:RB-P35-V01/RB-P35-V03','docs/rules/source-extraction/faq-v1.2-source-extraction.json:FQ-P02-U03','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json:officialLocalSymbols'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-029-A','description':'The page-35 queen-head/blob-plus-style inline glyph is the Shoot skull/Critical result referenced by FAQ and triggers a Queen Health card whenever that exact result is dealt.','support':'FAQ explicitly says skull symbol, but no independent exact morphology match to a page-40 token has been established'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-029-B','description':'The glyph is only the Queen Hits track terminal-space marker; FAQ separately names the Shoot skull result without creating a global icon identity.','support':'the visual census binds the glyph spatially to the terminal space and plain-text extraction loses its identity'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-029-C','description':'Use another source-scoped lethal-result relation established by future official component/icon evidence.','support':'current evidence supports the trigger prose but not a page-40, color-wide, shape-wide, or global alias'}]},
        {'questionId':'SEM-Q-030','title':'Serious Wound draw, reveal, and face-up placement timing','decisionClass':'official-clarification-preferred','blocksRuleIds':SERIOUS_WOUND_QUESTION_BLOCKS['SEM-Q-030'],'plannedRuleIds':[],'defaultProhibited':True,'sourceEvidenceRefs':['docs/rulebooks/rulebook_text.txt:lines 2594–2600, 3790–3796','docs/rules/source-extraction/rulebook-visual-obligations.json:RB-P18-V03','docs/rules/semantics/serious-wound-source-index.json'],'alternatives':[{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-030-A','description':'Reveal the random face immediately after drawing, then place it face up in the leftmost eligible Health Section.','support':'the official placement visual shows a readable face, but prose does not state the reveal point'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-030-B','description':'Place the random card first, then reveal it only after placement and Health displacement.','support':'setup explicitly says face down while gain prose says draw/place without a reveal verb'},{'alternativeId':'SEM-Q-030-C','description':'Use another source-defined visibility/orientation sequence while keeping all unselected fronts and deck order hidden.','support':'no checked source states a complete draw-to-placement information policy'}]},
