        {'conflictId':'SC-015','title':'Deadly Claws badge applicability and branch bodies differ by source version','status':'resolved-by-authority','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':['SEM-ATTACK-394906-001','SEM-ATTACK-394907-001','SEM-ATTACK-394908-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-RULEBOOK','SRC-ATTACK-394906','SRC-ATTACK-394907','SRC-ATTACK-394908','SRC-BGA-INTRUDER-ATTACKS'],'difference':'TTS scans assign Adult+Drone to the Health panels and Queen to a multi-Wound branch; current official-visible/licensed variants assign Adult+Queen to Health and Drone to a different injured-state branch.','resolution':'The official-visible current Lose-2 occurrence controls its matched counterpart; otherwise exact TTS and licensed variants remain occurrence-scoped under the authority order and are never flattened by title.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-016','title':'Infecting Adult/Drone/Queen applicability differs between official and TTS','status':'resolved-by-authority','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':['SEM-ATTACK-394911-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-RULEBOOK','SRC-ATTACK-394911','SRC-BGA-INTRUDER-ATTACKS'],'difference':'The TTS scan assigns Adult+Queen to Lose 2 and Drone to Contamination/Larva placement; official page 32 and BGA assign Adult+Drone and Queen respectively.','resolution':'Official page-32 row alignment controls the current visible counterpart. Preserve the exact TTS badge projection and licensed record as separate variants.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-017','title':'Tail Attack Queen/Drone applicability differs between scan and licensed data','status':'resolved-by-authority','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':['SEM-ATTACK-394918-001','SEM-ATTACK-394919-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-ATTACK-394918','SRC-ATTACK-394919','SRC-BGA-INTRUDER-ATTACKS'],'difference':'The TTS scans assign Adult+Queen to the first panel and Drone to the lethal branch; BGA assigns Adult+Drone to the first panel and Queen to the lethal branch.','resolution':'The exact source-bound scan controls over licensed-digital secondary data for these occurrences; both variants remain verbatim and source scoped.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-018','title':'Fury scan omits the licensed attacking-Room scope','status':'unresolved','questionId':'SEM-Q-020','affectedRuleIds':['SEM-ATTACK-394909-001','SEM-ATTACK-394910-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-ATTACK-394909','SRC-ATTACK-394910','SRC-BGA-INTRUDER-ATTACKS','docs/rules/open-questions.md:SEM-Q-020'],'difference':'The scans say all Heavily Injured Characters die and all survivors gain cards with no Room qualifier; BGA says those Characters are in your Room and then affects each other Character there.','resolution':'No default; preserve literal scan scope, the licensed local-scope lead, and all alternatives in review-gates.json.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-019','title':'Official Queen Health example versus TTS one-card Repel face wording','status':'resolved-by-authority','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':['SEM-QUEEN-HEALTH-504100-717B23-001','SEM-QUEEN-HEALTH-504200-CA5827-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-RULEBOOK','SRC-QUEEN-HEALTH-504100-717B23','SRC-QUEEN-HEALTH-504200-CA5827'],'difference':'The official page-35 visible example prints “Discard 1 additional card.” above “Repel the Queen.”; the shared TTS face prints plural “additional cards.” and a preceding Character-draw condition. The official occurrence does not identify either duplicate TTS GUID.','resolution':'Official-primary wording and two-panel structure control only the exact current visible occurrence. Preserve both TTS physical copies, their shared bytes, punctuation/pluralization, and unresolved copy correspondence independently.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-020','title':'Queen Health Malfunction/Unreinforce scan versus licensed Malfunction-only row','status':'resolved-by-authority','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':['SEM-QUEEN-HEALTH-458100-6BA0A2-001'],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-QUEEN-HEALTH-458100-6BA0A2','SRC-BGA-QUEEN-HEALTH'],'difference':'The exact TTS face says “Place a Malfunction in the Queen’s Room. OR Unreinforce Queen’s Corridor.” The discard-3 licensed row says only “Place a <MALFUNCTION> in the Room with the Queen.”','resolution':'The source-bound component scan controls this exact physical occurrence over licensed-digital secondary data. Preserve the licensed QueenHealthCard12 row as a separate material variant; do not delete the scan branch or rewrite either wording.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-021','title':'Queen death on last discard versus empty deck','status':'unresolved','questionId':'SEM-Q-027','affectedRuleIds':['SEM-QUEEN-HEALTH-RESOLUTION-001','SEM-QUEEN-DEATH-001',*QUEEN_HEALTH_RULE_IDS],'evidenceRefs':['SRC-RULEBOOK','SRC-OBJECTIVE-HELP','docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json'],'difference':'Rulebook page 35 repeatedly triggers Queen death when the last Queen Health card is discarded and sequences the drawn-card discard after its bottom effect; both Objective Help occurrences say the Queen is dead when the Queen Health deck is empty, which can happen as soon as the final card is drawn.','resolution':'No default. SEM-Q-027 preserves draw-empty, additional-discard, bottom-effect, drawn-discard, death, and reset alternatives without changing either official occurrence.'},
        {'conflictId':'SC-022','title':'TTS conditional faces versus licensed schema and ordinal/copy boundary','status':'preserved-boundary','questionId':None,'affectedRuleIds':QUEEN_HEALTH_RULE_IDS,'evidenceRefs':['docs/rules/semantics/queen-health-source-index.json','SRC-BGA-QUEEN-HEALTH'],'difference':'Every TTS face includes “If the card was drawn by a Character” while QUEEN_CARDS_DATA stores only discard/effect fields. BGA keys 1–12 form twelve independent licensed rows, but their suffixes are not printed numbers or source-backed TTS deck order; duplicate Repel/Activate rows cannot be paired one-to-one with duplicate TTS GUIDs by ordinal.','resolution':'Retain all twelve TTS physical occurrences, ten asset tuples, and twelve BGA rows independently. Candidate sets use exact structured tuples and multiplicity only; they never become title, filename, ordinal, or arbitrary duplicate-copy identity joins.'},
